{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/config.py","reason":"add effective_status_map forward resolution over the S1 mapping core (lazy import)"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py","reason":"resolve project key once; thread effective status_map into the CREATE/UPDATE Protocol calls and the status-annotation label diff"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_field_diff.py","reason":"compute_update_fields accepts and forwards status_map to map_fields_to_remote"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_backend.py","reason":"OutboundMapper Protocol: optional status_map on map_local_to_remote and map_fields_to_remote"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","reason":"Cloud backend wrappers forward status_map to the shared mapper / outbound_fields"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py","reason":"DC backend wrappers forward status_map; _map_local_to_dc_fields uses it for DC CREATE with built-in fallback and drift-omit"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py","reason":"shared map_fields_to_remote uses status_map (UPDATE, Cloud+DC); drift-omit on unmapped; built-in fallback"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/outbound_fields.py","reason":"_map_local_to_jira_fields uses status_map for Cloud CREATE; drift-omit; built-in fallback"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_labels.py","reason":"generalised rebar-status stamp rule keyed on built-in config.jira_to_local_status over the effective forward map"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_fields.py","reason":"generalised rebar-status:<local> label recovery via a shared parse helper; plain built-in reverse lookup unchanged"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py","reason":"use the shared rebar-status parse helper; retire the duplicated _REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_events.py","reason":"use the shared rebar-status parse helper; retire the duplicated literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_differ.py","reason":"use the shared rebar-status parse helper in place of the imported literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"re-export the shared parse helper in __all__ in place of the retired literal"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/fetcher.py","reason":"widen _known_jira_statuses to built-in plus config-declared Jira status names so a config-only status is not flagged unmapped"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_status_mapping.py","reason":"new behavioral oracle: config-effect, drift, remap/collapse round-trip, fetcher known-set, label-helper single-source"}]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"FILE_IMPACT","timestamp":1787335845252455001,"uuid":"4c123aad-1d33-471b-a979-b87805bc0182"}